WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.964 --> 00:00:19.687
I wasn't sure how long I'd been at Birtwick Park, for horses don't keep track of time the

2
00:00:19.727 --> 00:00:20.467
way humans do.

3
00:00:22.089 --> 00:00:25.551
But it had been long enough for everything about the place to feel familiar.

4
00:00:27.332 --> 00:00:30.094
I was used to my life there, and to the horses and people.

5
00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:32.876
I never expected anything to change.

6
00:00:36.076 --> 00:00:38.077
Then one day the squire came to the stable.

7
00:00:39.077 --> 00:00:41.498
John Manly had just ridden me out for some exercise.

8
00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:47.060
Now he was grooming me while James fetched some oats from the shed where the horses' feed was

9
00:00:47.121 --> 00:00:51.402
stored. When the squire came over, his face was serious.

10
00:00:53.183 --> 00:00:54.083
He was holding a letter.

11
00:00:55.664 --> 00:00:58.265
John immediately noticed the squire's serious face.

12
00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.407
He quickly led me into my stall and shut the door behind me.

13
00:01:04.047 --> 00:01:05.428
Then he turned to face the squire.

14
00:01:06.776 --> 00:01:08.197
"Good morning, sir," he said.

15
00:01:08.217 --> 00:01:09.778
"What can I do for you?"

16
00:01:09.798 --> 00:01:11.599
"Good morning, John."

17
00:01:12.399 --> 00:01:14.720
The squire's voice was as serious as his face.

18
00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.442
"I need to ask you something.

19
00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:20.484
Do you have any complaints about young James?"

20
00:01:21.744 --> 00:01:24.166
James himself had just emerged from the feed shed.

21
00:01:25.486 --> 00:01:27.648
He stood there in the doorway looking surprised.

22
00:01:29.108 --> 00:01:30.429
But John was quick to answer.

23
00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:32.690
"Complaints, sir?"

24
00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:33.431
he said.

25
00:01:33.451 --> 00:01:35.132
"Absolutely not."

26
00:01:36.412 --> 00:01:37.373
"Is he a hard worker?"

27
00:01:37.693 --> 00:01:38.594
the squire asked.

28
00:01:38.614 --> 00:01:41.617
"Or does he get lazy when your back is turned?"

29
00:01:42.618 --> 00:01:44.700
"He works as hard as I do," John said.

30
00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.562
"I've never known him to be lazy about anything."

31
00:01:49.164 --> 00:01:49.904
"That's good."

32
00:01:50.765 --> 00:01:52.767
The squire glanced at the letter he was holding.

33
00:01:52.787 --> 00:01:55.649
"But now I have another question for you.

34
00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:01.334
When he goes out with the horses to exercise them or to deliver a message, does he do

35
00:02:01.555 --> 00:02:02.876
only what he's supposed to be doing?

36
00:02:04.036 --> 00:02:06.698
Or do you think he might sometimes stop to talk with his friends?"

37
00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.342
"I have no reason to suspect that," John said, frowning.

38
00:02:11.362 --> 00:02:16.547
"And if anybody has been saying that sort of thing about James, I want to know who it

39
00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:22.472
is. James is the most honest young man I know, and the hardest worker too.

40
00:02:23.913 --> 00:02:28.316
He's gentle and clever with the horses, and I never worry about leaving him in charge when I

41
00:02:28.356 --> 00:02:29.157
have to go somewhere.

42
00:02:30.238 --> 00:02:32.380
If anyone wants to say otherwise, send him to me!"

43
00:02:33.408 --> 00:02:35.250
The squire's serious look disappeared.

44
00:02:36.651 --> 00:02:38.372
He chuckled and glanced over at James.

45
00:02:38.392 --> 00:02:41.795
"Come on out, young man," he said to him.

46
00:02:41.815 --> 00:02:46.339
"I'm glad to hear that John's opinion of you is the same as my own.

47
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.321
Now let me tell you why I needed to hear it."

48
00:02:51.343 --> 00:02:52.604
James came out to the yard.

49
00:02:54.005 --> 00:02:54.826
He looked nervous.

50
00:02:55.847 --> 00:02:56.567
"What is it, sir?"

51
00:02:56.928 --> 00:02:57.468
he asked.

52
00:02:57.488 --> 00:03:01.832
"Has someone been saying bad things about me?"

53
00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:05.450
"Not at all, my boy," the squire assured him.

54
00:03:06.531 --> 00:03:07.591
"I'm sorry to worry you.

55
00:03:08.412 --> 00:03:10.854
But I needed to make sure I got John's honest opinion.

56
00:03:12.355 --> 00:03:14.576
You see, my brother-in-law just wrote to me."

57
00:03:15.457 --> 00:03:16.277
He held up the letter.

58
00:03:17.658 --> 00:03:20.400
Then he explained that his brother-in-law was looking for a groom.

59
00:03:21.421 --> 00:03:24.523
"His old coachman has been with him for thirty years," he went on.

60
00:03:24.543 --> 00:03:28.826
"He wants a young man to work with him for a few years and take over when he

61
00:03:28.866 --> 00:03:33.702
retires. It would be a good job, with a fair salary and a nice place to live."

62
00:03:35.403 --> 00:03:37.004
"Oh," John said slowly.

63
00:03:37.024 --> 00:03:38.285
"I see.

64
00:03:39.266 --> 00:03:41.667
Well, I'll miss James if he takes the job, sir.

65
00:03:43.048 --> 00:03:45.710
But nobody deserves a good opportunity more than he does."

66
00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:48.552
"I agree," the squire said.

67
00:03:48.572 --> 00:03:50.914
"So do you think he can do the job?"

68
00:03:53.756 --> 00:03:55.457
"Yes, I do," John replied.

69
00:03:55.477 --> 00:03:58.980
"He doesn't have much experience in driving yet.

70
00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:03.354
But he can do everything else there is to do around the stable, and do it well.

71
00:04:04.555 --> 00:04:08.798
Your brother-in-law would be lucky to have him."

72
00:04:08.858 --> 00:04:10.619
I was listening along with the other horses.

73
00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:15.202
At first I didn't understand all of what the men were saying.

74
00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:20.625
But Merrylegs, who understands humans better than any of us, figured it out.

75
00:04:21.906 --> 00:04:25.208
James was going to be leaving us in about a month to work at another stable.

76
00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:30.294
In the meantime he needed practice driving the carriage as much as he could.

77
00:04:35.037 --> 00:04:38.359
For the next few weeks, the carriage went out more than ever before.

78
00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.542
Normally the squire only used it when his wife was going somewhere with him.

79
00:04:44.843 --> 00:04:48.765
But now Ginger and I were hitched to the carriage for every errand, no matter how small.

80
00:04:50.086 --> 00:04:53.168
At first John rode along to give instructions while James drove.

81
00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.883
After a while James was allowed to take us out by himself.

82
00:04:59.784 --> 00:05:01.525
His driving got better all the time.

83
00:05:03.908 --> 00:05:06.710
Finally the squire decided it was time for the final test.

84
00:05:07.791 --> 00:05:11.735
He and his wife wanted to pay a visit to some friends who lived about fifty miles away.

85
00:05:13.117 --> 00:05:16.440
It would be a two-day trip, and James would drive them there and back.
